1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,380
This is Canary.

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:08,520
A small yellow board that sits beside a lithium battery while it charges, and notices trouble before there is any smoke.

3
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:15,773
E-bike and scooter batteries get charged in hallways and bedrooms, often overnight.

4
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,933
When a cell fails, it does not start with smoke.

5
00:00:19,293 --> 00:00:20,593
It starts with a vent:

6
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:24,553
the electrolyte boils off as solvent vapour and carbon dioxide.

7
00:00:25,393 --> 00:00:28,373
Then the cell heats itself, runs away, and burns.

8
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:35,433
A smoke alarm only reacts at the very end of that chain, when the fire may already be between you and the door.

9
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:43,220
Grid storage batteries and electric car packs already carry off-gas detectors for exactly this.

10
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,160
The battery in your hallway has nothing.

11
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,800
So I designed one you can order fully assembled.

12
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:51,827
Here it is.

13
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:59,527
Sixty by forty millimetres, two copper layers, and every part on the top side, so the factory assembles it in a single pass.

14
00:01:00,187 --> 00:01:03,087
Power comes in over USB-C, from any phone charger.

15
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:10,987
An At-mega three twenty-eight P runs the firmware.

16
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:16,607
On the right, behind a slot that keeps the board's own warmth away, is the sensor head:

17
00:01:16,707 --> 00:01:24,187
a Sensirion SGP40 metal-oxide gas sensor, which reacts to solvent vapour, and an SHT40 for humidity and air temperature.

18
00:01:23,887 --> 00:01:29,707
In the middle sits a Sensirion SCD41, a photoacoustic carbon dioxide sensor.

19
00:01:29,407 --> 00:01:38,547
Bottom left is the thermal tab, another island cut free by slots, with copper on both faces and a one percent thermistor.

20
00:01:38,247 --> 00:01:42,547
Lay the board on the pack, and the tab reads the pack's skin temperature.

21
00:01:42,247 --> 00:01:48,067
If the pack charges inside the frame, a remote probe plugs into the connector beside it.

22
00:01:47,767 --> 00:01:48,507
Up top:

23
00:01:48,207 --> 00:01:54,007
a one hundred decibel sounder, three status lights, and a test and hush button.

24
00:01:57,067 --> 00:01:58,947
The firmware never trusts a single sensor.

25
00:01:58,647 --> 00:02:01,547
Cleaning spray trips the gas sensor.

26
00:02:01,247 --> 00:02:04,607
Someone breathing nearby raises carbon dioxide.

27
00:02:04,307 --> 00:02:07,347
A warm room warms the pack.

28
00:02:07,047 --> 00:02:11,607
Each of those is one kind of evidence, and earns an amber warning at most.

29
00:02:11,307 --> 00:02:13,607
A venting cell is different.

30
00:02:13,307 --> 00:02:19,427
Solvent vapour and carbon dioxide arrive together, and then the pack starts to heat.

31
00:02:19,127 --> 00:02:26,467
Two kinds of evidence at once, or a pack heating faster than three degrees a minute, and Canary goes to full alarm.

32
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:41,140
To prove the firmware, I ran the real compiled binary on a simulated At-mega chip, with virtual Sensirion sensors on its I2C bus, speaking their datasheet commands, and played scenarios into it.

33
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:44,720
Here a cell vents at the four hundred second mark.

34
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:55,960
The gas signal plunges, carbon dioxide climbs, and seven and a half seconds later the red light flashes, and the sounder starts the three-pulse pattern that smoke alarms use, at four kilohertz.

35
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,600
Everything is generated from code, and checked.

36
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:04,860
The schematic passes the electrical rules check with zero violations.

37
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:15,060
The board passes design rules with zero errors, zero warnings and zero unconnected pads, against P C B Way's own limits.

38
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:21,900
Fifty-six hardware-in-the-loop checks pass across eight scenarios, and a SPICE model shows the sounder driver stays clamped just above the supply.

39
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:36,440
To get one, upload the Gerber zip, the bill of materials and the placement file to P C B Way, ask them to flash the included firmware, and plug it into a USB charger.

40
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:37,800
One honest caveat.

41
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:45,740
The thresholds follow how venting cells are known to behave, but they have not yet been tested against a real cell venting beside this board.

42
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:47,280
That test comes next.

43
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:51,440
Until then, Canary is an early warning, not a certified alarm.

44
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:52,160
Keep your smoke alarm.

45
00:03:54,433 --> 00:03:55,113
Canary.

46
00:03:55,293 --> 00:03:57,833
Hear the battery, before you smell the smoke.

